{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"life support\" (+ mars moon planet planets) (+ habitat habitats colony colonies) (+ oxygen water food radiation))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_50_2338494947#9_3133992953","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3711","rank":1,"snippet":"yet? Why have we not sent a manned mission to Mars yet? Philip Rabe \" , \"segment\": \"And that’s because it would be very expensive, very dangerous, and reliant on undeveloped technologies and untested ideas. You can’t put people on Mars without putting a whole environment on Mars. They’d need to be carrying enough supplies to last for a 7 month trip plus a 1.5 year camp-out - they’d need a <cover>habitat, some way of getting into the landscape, protection from radiation, all the time living on can’t-fail life support systems. Continue Reading There have been clever little buggies weighed down with science gizmos driving around on Mars </cover>for ages. You mean why haven’t we been able to land people on Mars. And that’s because it would be very expensive, very dangerous, and reliant on undeveloped technologies and untested ideas. You can’t put people on Mars without putting a whole environment on Mars. They’d need to be carrying enough supplies to last for a 7 month trip plus a 1.5 year camp-out - they’d need a habitat, some way of getting into the "}}
