{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_50_735044610#16_1448576255","relevance":2,"reason":"The result is directly about whether Mars can support human life and mentions sufficient supplies, habitat atmosphere, and excess oxygen, but it appears to be a Quora discussion and the answer is partial rather than a dedicated, authoritative explanation of how to support life on other planets.","learned":"A proposed Mars base must have adequate supplies and carefully manage habitat atmosphere; excess oxygen and material depletion can threaten crew survival."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ nasa mars astronauts (+ need require) (+ oxygen water food shelter) (+ radiation \"life support\"))","reason":"Look for NASA educational or mission-planning pages that explicitly list what astronauts need to live on Mars, likely to be grade-3 evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ nasa mars astronauts (+ need require) (+ oxygen water food shelter) (+ radiation \"life support\"))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_118538044#2_201198654","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3714","rank":1,"snippet":"each morning with coffee and the Daily Brief (BYO coffee). \" , \"segment\": \"While Monday’s healthy snack won’t likely be particularly filling for the astronauts, it could pave the way to future crops grown on the space station and even other planets. As NASA and other space agencies look into longer missions to distant places like <cover>Mars, they will need to develop ways for astronauts to sustain themselves along the way, and when they get there. “There is evidence that supports fresh foods, such as tomatoes, blueberries and red lettuce, are a good source of antioxidants,” Ray Wheeler, the project’s lead researcher, told NASA’s website. “ Having fresh food like these available in space could have a positive impact on people’s moods and also could provide some protection against radiation </cover>in space.” NASA An artist’s rendering of what Martian gardening might look like, assuming no dust ever kicks up. NASA said it hopes ”space gardening” will become a “valued feature of life aboard the space station and in the future on Mars.” Add a green thumb to the long list of traits you’ll need in the future to become an "}}
