{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ nasa \"living on mars\" (+ astronauts humans) (+ oxygen water food shelter radiation))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_12_1623927183#6_3237808538","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3715","rank":1,"snippet":"25% 0% 0.5x 1x 1.25x 1.5x 2x facebook twitter Email Link https://bigthink.com/laurie-vazquez/the-2-biggest-challenges-humans-need-to-solve-before-living-on-mars?jwsource=cl Copied Embed <iframe src=\"//content.jwplatform.com/players/sNIg2sKM-FvQKszTI.html\" width=\"640\" height=\"360\" frameborder=\"0\" scrolling=\"auto\"></iframe> Copied Live 00:00 04:59 04:59 PROBLEM 2: Radiation Another problem with Mars’ thin atmosphere? Radiation – and it’s a doozy. Richard Davis, Assistant Director for Science and Exploration in <cover>NASA’s Planetary Science Division, explained it to The Week this way: “ A longer-term hazard [to humans living on Mars] is the general exposure to higher levels of radiation </cover>whether it be from the sun or sources external to the solar system. We can minimize these effects, but there will be increased exposure and thus a higher risk of cancer later in life.”\" , \"start_char\": 2998.000000 , \"title\": \"Want to Live on Mars? First We'll Have to Solve These Two Big Problems - Big Think\" , \"url\": \"https://bigthink.com/laurie-vazquez/the-2-biggest-challenges-humans-"}}
