{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_12_1623927183#6_3237808538","relevance":2,"reason":"The document is about obstacles to living on Mars and gives direct evidence that radiation exposure is a major human-survival problem, but the snippet only covers one hazard and the page is not clearly a comprehensive life-support answer.","learned":"Long-term human life on Mars requires mitigating higher radiation exposure from the Sun and outside the solar system."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"support life\" \"other planets\" (+ oxygen water food shelter habitat radiation))","reason":"Search the exact information-need wording plus concrete requirements to find documents dedicated to how life could be supported on planets beyond Earth."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"support life\" \"other planets\" (+ oxygen water food shelter habitat radiation))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_936325965#3_2104414755","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3716","rank":1,"snippet":"pee recycled into sugary drink 6. Monkey-like robot designed for rescue missions 7. Ice volcanoes on Pluto Additional Resources Red Planet Join Our Newsletter \" , \"segment\": \"Six Earth-like planets that might be able to accommodate life Are we the only sentient beings in the universe? It’s a question typically asked by conspiracy theorists and science fiction authors; NASA’s not known for chasing aliens and UFOs. But the Kepler mission aims to discover terrestrial planets, especially those that might have <cover>water and might be able to support life. Before the massive amount of exoplanets were discovered, the Kepler mission identified six other planets </cover>in the “habitable zone” of their suns. Two are rocky like Earth, and three could contain liquid water. Science Mission Directorate associate administrator John Grunsfeld said, “Each result from the planet-hunting Kepler mission’s treasure trove of data takes us another step closer to answering the question of whether we are alone in the Universe.” Sounds like maybe they could be searching for aliens after all. Thank you! Keep an eye out for our weekly newsletter.\" , \"start_char\": 3928.000000 ,"}}
