{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_07_1228747009#6_2221004676","relevance":3,"reason":"This FAQ is directly about whether Mars astronauts will have enough water, food, and oxygen and describes a Surface Habitat Environmental Control and Life Support System that creates a safe environment, supplies clean air and water, recycles wastes, and supports food production.","learned":"A Mars habitat can support humans through ECLSS that supplies clean air and water, recycles wastes, uses greenhouse food production, and stores emergency rations until resupply."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3719","reason":"The current query produced a grade-3 life-support result; continue it to find more documents specifically about Mars habitat life-support systems."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3719"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_07_1228747009#5_2221002655","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3719","rank":2,"snippet":"Any plant production surplus will be stored as emergency rations for the second crew and for emergencies. Non-edible parts of the plants will be recycled or stored until more advanced recycling equipment is shipped from Earth. Mars One will investigate the volume requirements for food production in the simulation outpost and the crews will be trained for many years to operate the greenhouse equipment. The aim is for colony to be independent from the food they receive from Earth. There will always be enough emergency rations in storage, locally produced or from Earth, to survive until the next supply mission comes. How to keep humans alive on Mars - Independent Surface Habitat ECLSS Conceptual Design Assessment by Paragon Mars One released a conceptual design report of the Surface Habitat Environmental Control and <cover>Life Support Systems (ECLSS) performed by Paragon Space Development Corporation.\" , \"start_char\": 2398.000000 , \"title\": \"Will the astronauts have enough water, food and oxygen? - Health and Ethics - Mars </cover>One\" , \"url\": \"http://www.mars-one.com/faq/health-and-ethics/will-the-astronauts-have-enough-water-food-and-oxygen\" }"}}
