{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_47_937424703#2_2027500616","relevance":3,"reason":"This document is directly about NASA's MOXIE technology converting Martian carbon dioxide into oxygen to help astronauts breathe on Mars, explaining that astronauts likely cannot bring enough oxygen and must produce it locally for breathing and return-rocket fuel.","learned":"A key way to support humans on Mars is in-situ oxygen production: MOXIE demonstrates converting carbon dioxide from the Martian atmosphere into oxygen for breathing and propellant."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3723","reason":"The oxygen-generation query produced strong direct evidence; continue to find additional NASA or technical results on making oxygen from the Martian atmosphere for human life support."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3723"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_47_937424703#3_2027502579","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3723","rank":2,"snippet":"NASA's Perseverance rover just turned CO2 into oxygen. The technology could help astronauts breathe on Mars. How MOXIE pulls oxygen out of thin air \" , \"segment\": \"Oxygen takes up a lot of room on a spacecraft, and it's unlikely that astronauts will be able to bring enough with them to Mars. So they'll need to produce their own oxygen from the Martian atmosphere, both for breathing and for fueling rockets to return to Earth. © JPL/NASA An artist's concept of <cover>astronauts and human habitats on Mars. JPL/NASA \"This is a critical first step at converting carbon dioxide to oxygen </cover>on Mars,\" Jim Reuter, the associate administrator for NASA's Space Technology Mission Directorate, said in a Wednesday press release. Load Error \"MOXIE has more work to do, but the results from this technology demonstration are full of promise as we move toward our goal of one day seeing humans on Mars,\" he added. \" Oxygen isn't just the stuff we breathe. Rocket propellant depends on oxygen, and future explorers will depend on producing propellant on Mars to make the trip home.\" The golden box holding the experiment is about "}}
