{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_960839854#3_1955518281","relevance":3,"reason":"This result directly explains ESA's MELiSSA closed-loop life-support system for astronauts exploring the Solar System, describing how waste such as urine and sweat can be recycled through filters, bioreactors, and chemical reactions to produce clean water, food, and oxygen for self-sufficiency.","learned":"Closed-loop bioregenerative life support can support humans away from Earth by recycling waste into the three basic elements of life: water, oxygen, and food."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3731","reason":"The MELiSSA query produced strong grade-3 evidence on closed-loop life support; continue to find more results about recycling waste into food, oxygen, and water for off-Earth habitats."}}
