{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_47_1388983668#11_2974474286","relevance":3,"reason":"This NASA page is directly dedicated to protecting astronauts from space radiation on Mars and gives concrete life-support/habitat evidence: radiation protection must be built into spacecraft, Martian habitats, and suits, with hydrogen-rich materials such as water, polyethylene, and processed trash tiles used as shielding.","learned":"Mars habitats can support human life by incorporating radiation shielding made from hydrogen-rich materials like water and plastics, potentially using already-required mass such as trash processed into protective tiles."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3732","reason":"The NASA radiation-protection query is producing dedicated grade-3 evidence on shielding and habitat design, so continue to retrieve more authoritative segments before switching topics."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3732"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_47_1388983668#1_2974454113","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3732","rank":3,"snippet":"technology. Today, as a result of extensive space radiation research, we have a much better understanding of our space environment, its effects, and the best ways to protect astronauts—all crucial parts of NASA's mission to send humans to Mars. \"The Martian\" film highlights the radiation dangers that could occur on a round trip to Mars. While the mission in the film is fictional, NASA has already started working on the technology to enable an actual trip to Mars in the 2030s. In the film, the astronauts’ habitat on Mars shields them from radiation, and indeed, radiation shielding will be a crucial technology for the voyage. From better shielding to advanced biomedical countermeasures, NASA currently studies how to protect astronauts and electronics from radiation – efforts that will have to be incorporated into every aspect of Mars mission planning, from spacecraft and <cover>habitat design to spacewalk protocols.\" , \"start_char\": 603.000000 , \"title\": \"How to Protect Astronauts from Space Radiation on Mars | NASA</cover>\" , \"url\": \"https://www.nasa.gov/feature/goddard/real-martians-how-to-protect-astronauts-from-space-radiation-on-mars\" }"}}
