{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_47_1388983668#8_2974468957","relevance":3,"reason":"This NASA page is dedicated to protecting astronauts from space radiation on Mars and provides direct evidence that galactic cosmic rays can create dangerous secondary radiation when they strike spacecraft, habitats, or vehicles, showing why radiation shielding and habitat design are essential for supporting human life on Mars.","learned":"Mars habitats, spacecraft, and vehicles must account for galactic cosmic rays and secondary radiation, which can reach dangerous levels and therefore require careful radiation-protection design."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3732","reason":"The NASA radiation-protection query has consistently produced dedicated grade-3 evidence on shielding, habitat design, and countermeasures needed to support humans on Mars."}}
